Two Neighbors, Same $1,000 Bonus. Only One Was Happier a Year Later
Narration script, about 870 words (about 6:00 with chart pauses).
Speakers: Narrator (Ren) throughout. Numbers are written out as spoken.
Lines marked [VERIFY] must be backed by a confirmed source, or removed.
Scene 1: Hook (0:00–0:30)
"Meet Max and Lena. Same street. Same salary. And on the same Friday, they both open an envelope with a one thousand dollar bonus inside. A year from now, one of them will barely remember what they spent it on. The other will still be feeling the benefit every single week. Same money. Completely different results. So what did Lena know that Max didn't?"
